# REQUIRES: verilator
# (11-08: the runs pin --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct, the defaults before then, so that the
# link counts and registers checked below stay those of the feature under test.)
# HBM link streams (`--link-kinds <producer>:<reader>:hbm`): the early links
# from one producer class to one reader class kept in device memory behind a
# virtual memory of one image (INSTANCES 1), a row a single address, the
# request's tag a landing slot. The producer's bits the links read are held
# at its pass and written a row a host cycle after it; each reader pass's
# rows (Reader reads two Units' rows: two landings a pass) are requested
# `lead` positions ahead and land over the host cycles before its slot, a
# bubble where a landing's response is late. Exact against the target
# (Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv: the virtual memories' model, rows zero at start,
# answered 1 to 60 host cycles on, `free` low at times), channels stalled or
# not, with bubbles; one stream alone; and the report's stream lines.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkhbm
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/two --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=TWO
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/two/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/two -DVM1 -Mdir %t/two/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/two/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/two/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/two/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/bub --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/bub.log 2>&1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/bub -DVM1 -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/bub/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/bub/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/bub/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+5 +bubble=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/bub/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+6 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/one --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/one.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONE < %t/one/schedule.txt
# A shorter lead (--link-hbm-lead): requests 10 positions ahead (the fewest: the decisions in flight + 6), more bubbles, as exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/lead --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-lead 10 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/lead.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LEAD < %t/lead/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/lead -DVM1 -Mdir %t/lead/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/lead/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/lead/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/lead/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=8 +hi=40 | FileCheck %s
# --link-hbm-min-lead: a member with less room from its row's write to its
# landing than that is an on-chip link (its landing would wait for the
# memory's round trip every frame): of Unit -> Reader's two members, the one
# with room 10 stays on chip at 11, and the stream's lead is the other's.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/minl --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 11 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/minl.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MINL < %t/minl/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/minl -DVM1 -Mdir %t/minl/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/minl/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/minl/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/minl/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+7 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# A stream none of whose members is kept builds nothing, so its ports space
# no pass: it is excluded and the frame scheduled again without it. At 100
# no member has the room: both streams excluded, the frame the stream-free
# fold's (no hbm rule; before, II 64 against 16: the dropped streams' ports
# still spaced the passes), every link on chip, exact. At 20 Reader -> Unit
# keeps none: excluded, and Unit -> Reader's members planned anew on the
# frame without its spacing (both kept, lead 40), exact.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/free --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo Unit Reader > %t/free.log 2>&1
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/drop --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 100 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/drop.log 2>&1
# RUN: cat %t/free.log %t/drop.log | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROP
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROPX < %t/drop.log
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -Mdir %t/drop/obj %S/Inputs/tb_reset.sv top.sv %t/drop/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/drop/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/drop/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/drop/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/drop1 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-min-lead 20 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=DROP1
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/drop1 -Mdir %t/drop1/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/drop1/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/drop1/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/drop1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/drop1/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# DROP: II = [[II:[0-9]+]]{{$}}
# DROP: II = [[II]]{{$}}
# DROP: link streams: 0 streams, 0 links, 0 bits
# DROPX: link stream Reader -> Unit keeps no member
# DROPX: link stream Unit -> Reader keeps no member
# DROP1: link stream Reader -> Unit keeps no member
# DROP1-NOT: Unit -> Reader keeps no member
# DROP1: link streams: 1 streams, 2 links
# DROP1: link stream Unit Reader 2 0 32 32 1 16 32 2 40{{$}}
# --link-hbm-row-bits: a stream's row (its controller's data width) at most
# that many bits; a wider word is cut into rows, written one a host cycle
# after the producer's pass and landing one a host cycle before the
# reader's (16: two rows a 32-bit word, the passes spaced, a longer frame).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rowb --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-hbm-row-bits 16 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/rowb.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWB < %t/rowb/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/rowb -DVM1 -Mdir %t/rowb/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/rowb/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rowb/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rowb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rowb/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: not foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rowbad --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --link-hbm-row-bits 5000 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ROWBAD
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/one -Mdir %t/one/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/one/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/one/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/one/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# A staged reader (--stage-levels: Reader evaluates over its stages, its links
# read its stages before its state pass): its landings precede that read.
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/stg --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --bubbles --stage-levels 1 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=STG
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/stg -DBUBBLES -Mdir %t/stg/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/stg/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/stg/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/stg/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+3 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/stg/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+4 +bubble=30 +stall=30 +lo=1 +hi=20 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# STG: Reader staged: 2 stages
# Two reader copies: a stream with a member dropped (its row written after the
# reads the stream would request of it) requests only its kept members' rows
# (before, the dropped row's read went out ahead of its write: PROTOCOL).
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/rc2 --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --copies Reader:2 --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm Unit Reader > %t/rc2.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RC2 < %t/rc2/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/rc2 -DVM1 -DVM2 -DVM3 -Mdir %t/rc2/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/rc2/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/rc2/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/rc2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=60 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/rc2/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=20 +stall=30 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# RC2: link stream {{.+}} 1 1 32
# A late producer (Driver/Inputs/linklate: each unit's output passes its input
# through) is no stream's: its readers take it in the frame it is written, and
# a stream lands a frame on. The streams are laid out after the analysis that
# marks it late (before, it was a member and the fold mismatched).
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linklate && foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/late --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=LATE
# LATE: II =
# LATE-NOT: link stream
# A stream of 26 pages (Driver/Inputs/linkwide: a 13,000-bit word) behind a
# controller of 32 entries' room: its page writes are at positions, one a
# position, so it asks no more room than the decisions in flight take (before,
# pages + 1 more: never there, no position ran).
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkwide && foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/wide --static --no-drop-dead-inputs --no-staged-link-direct --nest --modulo --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm Unit Reader 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=WIDE
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkwide && %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/wide -Mdir %t/wide/obj %S/Inputs/tb_linkhbm.sv top.sv %t/wide/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/wide/build.log 2>&1
# RUN: %t/wide/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+1 +lo=1 +hi=20 +room=32 | FileCheck %s
# RUN: %t/wide/obj/Vtb +verilator+rand+reset+2 +verilator+seed+2 +lo=1 +hi=60 +room=32 +full=20 | FileCheck %s
# WIDE: link stream Unit Reader 1 0 13000 512 26
# TWO: II = 64
# TWO: link streams: 2 streams, 3 links, 2304 bits
# TWO: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 32 1 16 16 1 {{[0-9]+}}
# TWO: link stream Unit Reader 2 0 32 32 1 16 32 2
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_COUNT 2
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_TAGS
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_IW 7
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_INSTANCES 1
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_0_TAGW 6
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_INSTANCES 1
# VH: `define FOLDSIM_VMEM_1_TAGW 6
# ONE: link use Reader Unit 32 32 16 hbm 1
# ONE: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 32 1 16 16 1
# LEAD: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 32 1 16 16 1 10{{$}}
# MINL: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 32 1 16 16 1 11{{$}}
# ROWB: II = 80
# ROWB: link stream Reader Unit 1 0 32 16 2 32 32 2
# ROWB: link stream Unit Reader 1 1 32 16 2 32 32 2
# ROWBAD: link-hbm-row-bits: 5000 is not 8 to 4096
# MINL: link stream Unit Reader 1 1 32 32 1 16 16 1 48{{$}}
# CHECK: {{^}}MATCH 196 cycles
# CHECK-NOT: PROTOCOL
